From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-17x: Add the pixel pipeline (Bayer to NV12/NV21)

Upstream drives only the RDI write masters of Titan 17x. Add a fixed
parameter pixel pipeline on VFE_LINE_PIX for VFEs that describe pixel
pipeline output formats:

  CSID IPP -> CAMIF -> DEMUX -> DEMOSAIC (+WB) -> CST (BT.601 full range)
  -> FULL path MNDS (luma at compose size, chroma 4:2:0) -> CROP ->
  ROUND/CLAMP (8 bit) -> FULL Y (WM3) and FULL C (WM4)

Both write masters form bus composite group 0, so a frame completes
once, through the composite done IRQ, and their per master done bits
are ignored. The CAMIF reg update (command bit 0, done in status0 bit
4) latches the pipeline configuration and the buffer addresses of each
frame.

White balance gains are unity, directional demosaic interpolation is
off because it needs per sensor weights, and lens shading, colour
correction and gamma are bypassed.

Register offsets and field layouts come from the Titan 17x register
packing of the SC8280XP Windows camera stack (CamX rel 10.6
QcDeviceMFT8280.dll and the qccamisp8280.sys ISP driver). The CST
matrix is the one of the S5K3L6 chromatix tuning.

While at it, fix two issues in the ISR:
- Read the three bus IRQ status registers instead of line_num of them.
  With line_num == 4 the loop read VFE_BUS_IRQ_STATUS(3), which is
  VFE_BUS_IRQ_CLEAR_GLOBAL, and wrote VFE_BUS_IRQ_CLEAR(3), which is
  VFE_BUS_IRQ_STATUS(0).
- Report VFE violations. vfe_violation_read() had no caller.

